  {
   "heading": "Rank-2 temperaments",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "31edo provides the optimal patent val for the rank-5 temperament tempering out the 13-limit comma 66/65 , which equates 6/5 and 13/11 . It also provides the optimal patent val for mohajira, squares , and casablanca in the 11-limit, and huygens/meantone , squares, winston , lupercalia , and nightengale in the 13-limit.\n* Octave-reduced form , reduced to the first half-octave, and minimal form in parentheses if distinct"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Octave stretch or compression",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "31edo can benefit from slightly stretching the octave , especially when using it as an 11-limit equal temperament. With the right amount of stretch we can find a slightly better 3rd harmonic and significantly better 11th harmonic at the expense of somewhat less accurate approximations of 5, 7, and 13.\nWhat follows is a comparison of stretched-octave 31edo tunings.\nPure-octaves 31edo approximates all harmonics up to 16 within 11.1 ¢.\nStretching the octave of 31edo by around 0.5 ¢ results in slightly improved primes 3, 7 and 11, but slightly worse primes 2, 5 and 13. This approximates all harmonics up to 16 within 12.8 ¢. Both the 13-limit TE and WE tunings do this.\nStretching the octave of 31edo by around 0.8 ¢ results in slightly improved primes 3 and 11, but slightly worse primes 2, 5, 7 and 13. This approximates all harmonics up to 16 within 14.2 ¢. The tuning 127zpi does this.\nStretching the octave of 31edo by around 1.2 ¢ results in slightly improved primes 3 and 11, but slightly worse primes 2, 5 and 7, and much worse 13. This approximates all harmonics up to 16 within 15.5 ¢ Its 11-limit WE tuning and 11-limit TE tuning both do this, so does the tuning 111ed12 .\nStretching the octave of 31edo by around 2.0 ¢ results in slightly improved primes 3 and 11, but slightly worse primes 2, 5 and 7, and much worse 13. This is approaching 2.239 ¢ – the most octave stretch 31edo can tolerate before the mapping of the 13th harmonic changes. This approximates all harmonics up to 16 within 18.5 ¢. The tuning 80ed6 does this.\nStretching the octave of 31edo by around 3.3 ¢ results in improved primes 3 and 11, especially 11, but slightly worse primes 2, 5, 7 and 13. The 13 is now differently mapped than – and much better than – 80ed6's (but not as good as the pure octaves 13). This approximates all harmonics up to 16 within 15.6 ¢. The tuning 49edt does this."
  },
