  {
   "heading": "MOS scales",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "The fact that 31edo has meantone diatonic and chromatic scales is well-known, but some other MOSes and MOS chains [ clarification needed ] are also useful:\nSee #Rank-2 temperaments for a table of MOSes and their temperament interpretations."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Harmonic scales",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "31edo approximates Mode 8 of the harmonic series okay, but many intervals between the harmonics aren't distinguished, most importantly 9/8 (major tone) and 10/9 (minor tone), as 31EDO is a meantone temperament. The interval between the 8th and 11th harmonics is approximated okay, but the intervals between the 11th harmonic and closer harmonics such as the 12th and 9th harmonics are approximated much better. 31edo's closest approximation of 13/8, the neutral sixth, is significantly sharper than just and only vaguely suggests the 13-limit .\nThe steps are: 5 5 4 4 4 3 3 3.\nIn mode 16, the most closely-matched harmonics are the composite ones, 21 and 25. Of the other harmonics:"
  },
